it for durable storage. Leader tracks Match per peer, aggregates only configured voters (both majorities in joint state), and commits a quorum-supported index only if it belongs to its term. Append/heartbeat propagates commitment, with heartbeat commit bounded by each follower Match. Ready delivers committed entries in order and completion responses advance applied and release quota. Rejection, heartbeat retry and snapshot fallback repair lagging support.',['B-replicate','B-storage','B-apply','B-recover'],['F-commit','F-config'],['s-send','s-replicate','s-resp','s-log-append','s-log-term','src-quorum','s-ready-advance']),context=path('A promotable node without unapplied committed configuration changes campaigns, optionally pre-voting. Votes require up-to-date history and compatible term/vote state; persisted replies are aggregated under installed voters. Winning becomes leader and appends a current-term empty entry. Higher terms normally become follower; pre-vote and active-lease checks have explicit exceptions. Reset clears volatile votes, progress, read-only support and transfer target but retains log/commit. Same-term leader traffic ends candidacy; old-term traffic cannot count as fresh replication support. Transfer temporarily blocks proposals, catches up its target and sends TimeoutNow; timeout clears transfer without changing role. Applying configuration updates quorum authority; snapshot/restart restore it.',['B-authority','B-transfer','B-config','B-recover'],['F-config','F-commit'],['src-transition','s-role','s-follower','s-resp','s-timer','src-config','src-recovery']),connection=path('Eligible support depends jointly on current term and installed membership. Role reset discards volatile replication/vote support, but retained committed history restricts future vote eligibility and append acceptance. Joint membership requires old and new majorities; applying a configuration can itself make more entries quorum-supported. Deferred storage acknowledgments are qualified by term, with committed snapshot/application completions surviving authority change. Pending proposal success is not guaranteed; proposals during transfer are dropped. Safe read support is rebuilt after reset and gated on current-term commit; queued pre-commit requests are separately released later. Application of committed membership plus applied progress conditionally initiates automatic exit; proposal acceptance is still governed by current authority/transfer state.',['B-authority','B-storage','B-config','B-apply','B-read','B-transfer'],['F-commit','F-config'],['src-transition','src-commit','src-config','src-auto','s-read-release','s-leader']),open_details=['Automatic exit retry after failed transfer without later application.','Cancellation documentation discrepancy.','Pending read context behavior across membership changes.','Deeper asynchronous snapshot and flow-control histories remain unexamined.'],core_gaps=[],rationale='Representative formation, authority, persistence, membership, recovery and consumption paths are traced with their guards and asynchronous boundaries; this is a usable partial map, not a coverage or correctness claim.'))\njson.dump(M,open('map.json','w'),indent=2)\nQ=dict(question='Can a legally applied implicit joint configuration remain without an automatic exit proposal after application completion attempts exit during leadership transfer, transfer later aborts, and no further application work is pending?',importance='A missed automatic exit can retain outgoing voters and obstruct subsequent membership changes or intended availability. No consensus safety violation is presumed.',source_ids=['src-auto','s-auto-contract','s-ready-advance','s-transfer-end','s-timer','s-leader','s-joint-interface'],participants=['Leader','Voter transferee','Quorum peers','Caller processing Ready'],objects=['Installed joint ConfState','Pending configuration index','Application completion','leadTransferee'],contexts=['Implicit joint configuration with 